Before even trying vmware, have a look at VirtualPC.

Microsoft bought it a while ago, so that they could help people migrate
to a new windows and keep their old machine running.

It is a free emulator, in the monetary sense (not free in the `free software'
sense, though) that you can download as you wish and play with.

It can boot other OSes, I went as far as to do a full OpenBSD install under
it. I haven't tried booting from an external HD, though.

Compared to VMWare and Linux, its main drawback would be that it only works
with Windows as host OS, as far as I know...


